Parts of the HomeKit implementation (the accessory protocol, camera streaming, HomeKit Secure Video and
the HomeKit Data Stream) were written with reference to these projects, under the Apache License 2.0
(licenses/Apache-2.0.txt):
- HAP-NodeJS (https://github.com/homebridge/HAP-NodeJS)
- HomeKitADK (https://github.com/apple/HomeKitADK)
Source files that follow one of them closely name it in a comment.

The built-in detection model (models/yolo26s.mlpackage, compiled into the app) is Ultralytics YOLO26
(https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics), Copyright Ultralytics, under the GNU Affero General Public
License v3.0, exported to Core ML. Other models can be used in its place (docs/detection.md).

Search's picture model (models/search/, built into released copies of the app) is Google's SigLIP 2 base
(google/siglip2-base-patch16-224, https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-base-patch16-224), under the Apache License
2.0 (licenses/Apache-2.0.txt). Pond converts it to Core ML and quantizes its weights (scripts/convert-siglip.py);
the converted model is a modification of the original.

Reolink's own protocol (Baichuan) was written with reference to reolink_aio
(https://github.com/starkillerOG/reolink_aio), under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 starkillerOG.
